NAME
       zip - pack files into a .zip archive

SYNOPSIS
       zip [-r] [-q] [-v] [-9] ARCHIVE.zip FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       zip creates ARCHIVE.zip (or adds to it) with the FILEs compressed
       inside. The .zip format is the one Windows and macOS open directly,
       so it is handy for sharing with other systems; for backups on Linux,
       tar keeps owners and permissions better. Directories are only
       included with -r. zip is in its own package, which is not installed
       by default.

OPTIONS
       -r     Include directories with everything in them.

       -q     Quiet.

       -v     Verbose.

       -9     Compress as much as possible (slower).

EXAMPLES
           zip -r /root/site.zip /var/www/html
           unzip -l /root/site.zip

SEE ALSO
       unzip(1), tar(1), gzip(1)
